{:fh/id  "FH-CTRL-014"
 :fh/law "RESET and REBASE are distinct transitions and neither is the other. Reset discards the draft back to the baseline, clears the leaf's visited / edited / error marks, and ADVANCES that leaf's reset revision — so a caller rejecting a draft by reasserting the value it already had is observable, which value-equality provably is not. Rebase moves the baseline under a live draft, KEEPS the draft, clears the edited mark only where the draft now agrees with the new baseline, and advances no revision, because a rebase is not a rejection. A scoped reset advances one leaf's generation and no other."

 :baseline {:amount "10" :notes "keep typing"}

 :amount-path [:amount]
 :notes-path  [:notes]

 :typed-amount "bad"
 :typed-notes  "half a sentence"

 ;; Every leaf starts at generation 0, so a control is fenced from its
 ;; first render rather than from its first rejection.
 :initial-reset-key 0

 ;; THE CASE THE WHOLE DESIGN EXISTS FOR. The caller refuses "bad" and
 ;; stands by "10" — the value it already had. Nothing derived from the
 ;; value can see that decision.
 :reasserted-value "10"

 ;; After a SCOPED reset of :amount.
 :amount-after-reset      "10"
 :amount-reset-key-after  1
 :notes-after-reset       "half a sentence"
 :notes-reset-key-after   0
 :edited-after-reset      #{[:notes]}

 ;; After a WHOLE-FORM reset every leaf's generation advances together and
 ;; every mark is cleared.
 :whole-form-reset-keys {[:amount] 2 [:notes] 1}
 :draft-after-whole-reset {:amount "10" :notes "keep typing"}
 :edited-after-whole-reset #{}

 ;; REBASE. The save landed and the domain accepted a new amount while the
 ;; user was still typing notes.
 :rebase-values {:amount "10"}

 ;; The draft STANDS — including the draft on the very leaf that was
 ;; rebased — and no generation moves.
 :draft-after-rebase       {:amount "bad" :notes "half a sentence"}
 :amount-reset-key-after-rebase 0

 ;; The edited mark clears only where the draft now AGREES with the new
 ;; baseline; there is nothing left to protect there.
 :agreeing-rebase-values {:amount "bad"}
 :edited-after-agreeing-rebase #{[:notes]}

 ;; THE CONTRAST, asserted as one table so the two transitions cannot be
 ;; green for the same reason.
 :reset-discards-draft? true
 :rebase-keeps-draft?   true
 :reset-advances-generation? true
 :rebase-advances-generation? false}
